1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,740
A business brief should become a document a
team can review, not a black box.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:11,428
This is Docentric Copilot: quotation in, two-page DOCX
out, with schema, validation and diff attached.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,943
Everything starts with the customer's data.

4
00:00:14,963 --> 00:00:20,915
Here is a synthetic DDSP package with thirty-four fields
across three sections and one repeating collection.

5
00:00:20,935 --> 00:00:24,364
Sample data and parser diagnostics are
included.

6
00:00:24,384 --> 00:00:29,716
The schema is normalized, so every field the
document can bind has a type and evidence.

7
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,720
Routing starts with complexity.

8
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:40,256
The workspace panel calls this quotation brief ambiguous,
recommends Anthropic under a thirty-cent budget, and asks
for human review.

9
00:00:40,276 --> 00:00:45,172
But recommendation is not execution; the
panel does not show which model ran.

10
00:00:45,192 --> 00:00:54,772
The live trace does: the benchmark's quotation case
executed gpt-6-sol, compiled, and passed the validation
gate in 19.4 seconds for 3.6 cents.

11
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:58,334
Six cases, three providers, one run per
case.

12
00:00:58,354 --> 00:01:06,501
gpt-6-sol and claude-sonnet-5-5 each produced six valid
templates out of six, with p50 latency of 19.0 and 14.2
seconds.

13
00:01:06,521 --> 00:01:10,240
Cost per valid template: 3.3 and 4.7 cents.

14
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:16,964
Gemini-3.1-flash-lite produced zero; its latency and cost
are unknown, so the slide shows N/A, never zero.

15
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:20,119
Download the DOCX and open it.

16
00:01:20,139 --> 00:01:25,132
The quotation is 40,585 bytes and two pages.

17
00:01:25,152 --> 00:01:31,341
On the left is the independent preview; on the right, page
one as rendered by LibreOffice.

18
00:01:31,361 --> 00:01:34,235
Both are labelled for what they are.

19
00:01:34,255 --> 00:01:39,636
This is a LibreOffice rendering, not a
Microsoft Word fidelity claim.

20
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,341
Here is the visual defect.

21
00:01:43,361 --> 00:01:49,869
The Description column is 62 millimetres at 9.5 points,
and two cells wrap past four estimated lines.

22
00:01:49,889 --> 00:01:53,005
Optimize layout applies typed IR changes.

23
00:01:53,025 --> 00:02:00,471
Description widens to 88.7 millimetres by rebalancing the
other columns, and the table font drops to 9.0 points.

24
00:02:00,491 --> 00:02:02,797
Seven IR fields change.

25
00:02:02,817 --> 00:02:08,144
The panel reruns the checks: text fit now passes, and the
after image uses fewer lines.

26
00:02:08,164 --> 00:02:11,628
LibreOffice rendering, not Word pagination.

27
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,390
Every edit creates an immutable version.

28
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:20,771
V1 to V2 changed five IR fields, added none
and removed none.

29
00:02:20,791 --> 00:02:27,292
The comparison names each changed path, and Restore
version brings either pane back into the workspace.

30
00:02:27,312 --> 00:02:30,676
Diff and rollback, not a silent edit.

31
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,867
Docentric Copilot is open source on GitHub
under Apache 2.0.

32
00:02:36,888 --> 00:02:41,280
The demo, the benchmark and the evidence are
in the repository.

33
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:45,084
Docentric AX compatibility: not tested.

